            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear Colleague, thank you for referring this 84-year-old male patient who was admitted on 16/01/2013 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray showed hyperinflation without consolidation. Blood tests and arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Spirometry supported severe obstructive ventilatory impairment. He was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Vital signs were monitored closely throughout his stay. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. Discharge education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation self-management was provided. Please arrange follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Yours sincerely.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
